## 21. No Implied Permissions

CleanroomMC License grants only the permissions expressly stated in it.

No additional right arises merely because:

- the Source can be viewed or downloaded;
- a repository is public;
- a technical system allows copying or forking;
- the Work contains a `public` API, class, method, field, or member;
- the project contains material under a more permissive licence;
- another Directory in the same repository uses another licence;
- the Licensor previously tolerated similar conduct; or
- exercising a restricted right would be convenient or technically necessary.

A permission granted by another licence applies only to material governed by that licence.

It must not be extended to Cleanroom-licensed material merely because the two are stored, compiled, packaged, distributed, or used together.

Where You need a right that CleanroomMC License does not expressly grant, You must obtain separate permission from the relevant copyright holder.
